<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"  xml:id="chapter-1-intro">
  <title>Week 1</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      At the end of this week you should be able to...
    </p>
    <objectives>
      <ul>
        <li>log in to a remote linux server with ssh</li>
        <li>change their password on a linux system</li>
        <li>view files on a linux system</li>
        <li>use jshell from the command-line</li>
        <li>use a REPL to evaluate simple expressions</li>
        <li>describe values of primitive types such as integers and floating point numbers</li>
        <li>understand what an expression is and how simple expressions are evaluated</li>
        <li>predict how arithmetic operators in java work over given values</li>
      </ul>
    </objectives>
  </introduction>
  <xi:include  href="sec-language-elements.ptx"/>
  <xi:include  href="sec-compiling.ptx"/>
  <xi:include  href="sec-expressions.ptx"/>
</chapter>
